{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research: how major Python projects avoid by-path module identity collisions (2026-08-10)\n\nThe closest production-grade precedent is pytest itself. Its centralized import_path implementation does four things our 209 duplicated loaders do not: (1) derives a unique sys.modules name from the file path relative to a root in importlib mode; (2) returns an already-loaded module cache-first; (3) verifies that the cached module's __file__ matches the requested path and raises ImportPathMismatchError when it does not; and (4) inserts the module into sys.modules before exec_module. Source: https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/main/src/_pytest/pathlib.py and https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/pythonpath.html#import-modes. The pytest docs explicitly say importlib mode generates a unique name from rootdir, while non-package test trees otherwise require globally unique module names.\n\nCPython centralizes intentional fresh-import behavior in Lib/test/support/import_helper.py. import_fresh_module and CleanImport save affected sys.modules entries, remove them for the test, and restore them afterward. It does not let individual tests permanently overwrite shared aliases. Source: https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Lib/test/support/import_helper.py\n\nThese are highly active/popular precedents as of 2026-08-10: CPython ~74K stars and pytest ~14K, both updated today. The common architecture is an importable test-support module with explicit module-cache semantics, not hundreds of local loaders and not a fixture-only abstraction.\n\nRecommended shape for rebar: tests/_support/import_path.py (inside an importable tests support package) callable at module scope and from fixtures. Give every source path a stable collision-free module name derived from its repository-relative path. If that name exists, return it only when resolved __file__ matches; otherwise fail loudly. Insert before exec and remove on failed execution. Provide a separate scoped fresh-import context that saves/restores sys.modules for the rare test that deliberately needs a second class identity. Do not silently overwrite a short shared name such as mutation or differ. This is broader and safer than merely adding cache-first checks to the existing aliases."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786395063963150001,"uuid":"2cafa68f-ad21-4745-b2c2-82333fd135ef"}